// The imagedecode package: pictures out of files, in Cone. PNG and JPEG
// decoders, and a PNG writer, with no C library: stb_image's and libpng's jobs
// for the 3-D browser's textures. The DEFLATE (zlib) reader and writer and the
// checksums they stand on live in the 'deflate' package, which this one imports
// and whose names it re-exports.
//
//   import imagedecode use *;
//
//   match decode(bytes) {                    // a PNG or a JPEG, whichever it is
//     case imm r Ok {
//       // r is a Raster: r.width, r.height, RGBA, rows from the TOP down,
//       // 8 bits a channel in r.pixels8 (16 in r.pixels16 for a 16-bit PNG)
//       imm img = new render.Image(r.width, r.height, 4, r.bottomUp(4));
//     }
//     case imm e Error { /* e.reason says why */ }
//   }
//
// render's Image is rows bottom-first, 8-bit, 3 or 4 channels; 'bottomUp'
// gives exactly that, so the hook into render's 'addTexture' (sRGB colour),
// 'addLinearTexture' and 'addNormalTexture' is the one line above, and mip
// levels are render's own ('mips.cone'). This package does not import
// render (that would link SDL3 into every tool that reads a picture).
//
// WHAT IS HERE
//
//   Raster         what a decode gives: always RGBA, 8 or 16 bits, colour not
//                  premultiplied, with what the file says about its colours
//                  (sRGB, gamma) and the Exif orientation a JPEG asked for.
//   decode         PNG or JPEG by the file's first bytes ('sniff' says which);
//                  BMP is render's Image.fromBmp; WebP and KTX2 are refused by
//                  name with the reason.
//   decodePng      every colour type at every bit depth (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),
//                  the five filters, Adam7 interlacing, tRNS (palette alpha,
//                  or a colour key), gAMA and sRGB recorded, every chunk's
//                  CRC checked. 16-bit pictures decode to RGBA16.
//   decodeJpeg     baseline, extended-sequential and progressive Huffman JPEG
//                  of 8-bit samples, one to four components, any sampling
//                  (4:4:4, 4:2:2, 4:2:0, 4:4:0, 4:1:1, odd ones), restart
//                  markers, JFIF, Adobe RGB / YCbCr / CMYK / YCCK, Exif
//                  orientation applied (or not, 'decodeJpegWith').
//   inflate, zlibDecompress     RFC 1951 and RFC 1950: stored, fixed and
//                  dynamic blocks; the Adler-32 checked. Re-exported from
//                  the deflate package (so are zlibCompress, adler32 and
//                  Crc32); the error is deflate's DeflateError, which has
//                  the 'reason' and 'message()' a DecodeError has.
//   deflate, zlibCompress       the other way: stored, fixed-Huffman and
//                  dynamic-Huffman at three levels (see the deflate package;
//                  'deflate' here is its 'rawDeflate', the name being the
//                  package's own there).
//   encodePng, encodePngSamples a Raster or raw samples written as a PNG, any
//                  colour type and depth, any filter or the adaptive choice,
//                  Adam7, tRNS, PLTE, gAMA, sRGB (so a screenshot or a baked
//                  texture can be saved).
//   adler32, Crc32 the checksums (deflate's).
//
// Every decoder takes bytes (an &Array[u8], which a &str also is) and answers
// a core Result: Ok or an Error holding a 'reason'. A damaged or hostile file
// is refused, never a panic: the fuzz test damages valid files tens of
// thousands of ways. A picture over 2^28 pixels, and an ask to inflate more
// than 1 GiB, are refused, and no allocation is made on a header's word
// before the data to fill it is seen (a PNG's inflate is limited to the size
// its header implies, and reserves at most 64 MiB up front).
//
// THE METHODS (each an industry-standard one, cited in its file)
//
//   Huffman decode, inflate,   in the deflate package (its header names them):
//   deflate (writing)          zlib's design for decoding, a greedy LZ77 with
//                              a three-byte hash chain for writing.
//   PNG                       the W3C specification, filters and Adam7 as
//                              written there; one pass over the inflated
//                              data in place.
//   JPEG                       libjpeg's: the "islow" integer IDCT, "fancy"
//                              (triangle) chroma upsampling and its 16-bit
//                              fixed-point YCbCr table, decoded
//                              coefficients first and pixels after, so
//                              progressive files share the path. The output
//                              is bit-identical to libjpeg-turbo's on the
//                              reference files of the test (largest
//                              difference 0).

// NOT HERE: arithmetic-coded, lossless, 12-bit or hierarchical JPEG; PNG
// APNG animation frames (the first frame decodes, as the PNG stream says);
// colour management (an ICC profile is ignored; sRGB and gAMA are only
// reported); GIF, WebP, KTX2, Basis.
//
// Speed, on a 2048 x 2048 picture (best of five, release build, i7-13700HX;
// examples/bench.cone): a PNG of 12.6 MB filtered RGB (4.4 MB compressed) in
// 277 ms, a 4:2:0 JPEG (0.7 MB) in 119 ms, a progressive one in 162 ms.
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports:
//
//   imagedecode.cone  this overview
//   raster.cone       Raster, ColorSpace
//   decode.cone       decode, sniff, DecodeError
//   zlib.cone         'deflate', the writer's old name for deflate's rawDeflate
//   png.cone         decodePng
//   pngwrite.cone     PngWrite, encodePng, encodePngSamples
//   jpeg.cone         the JPEG parser, Huffman and progressive decode
//   jpegout.cone      the IDCT, upsampling, colour, orientation

mod imagedecode;

import collections use *;
pub import deflate as flate use inflate, zlibDecompress, zlibCompress, adler32, Crc32;
